[COMMENTS]
STATION,Short-crested weir gauging a predominantly Millstone Grit catchment with urban lower reaches. GENERAL: Station opened August 2000 on an existing industrial short-crested weir under a bridge on a slight bend with long straight approach channel. STATION HYDROMETRY: Station not bypassed and not thought to drown. The higher flows have been gauged off a bridge upstream. Three peak flow ratings applied across period of record based on current meter gaugings and ADCP gaugings. Rating extrapolated beyond highest gauging using velocity extrapolation method. Radar level measurement installed in November 2023. FLOW RECORD: No data after 01/08/2022 pending instrument replacement. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11). FLOW REGIME: Station is just downstream of the Bradshaw Valley Reservoir system of Entwhistle, Wayoh, and Jumbles for water supply and compensation. The level / flow at Brashaw Tennis Club during low flows is heavily influenced by the outflow from Jumbles reservoir and can rise and fall very quickly depending on reservoir releases.
CATCHMENT,Geology of Millstone Grit overlain with peat moorland in headwaters, with Boulder Clay and coal measures in the urban lower parts. No catchment changes known.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged to moderate level, extrapolated by stage\hydraulic radius method.
Pooling Suitability,No high flow gaugings, limiting confidence in extrapolation.
[END]
